INT. DESALINATION PLATFORM "KESTREL REEF," DORMITORY GALLEY - NIGHT

A steel room bolted to the open sea. Portholes show black water and the white scrawl of waves. A table, three stools, a kettle that screams on a hotplate. Everything slightly damp.

PERPETUA LOWE, fifties, platform superintendent, scrapes burnt toast over the sink. YOSHIRO ABE, thirties, the pump engineer, sits slumped at the table with his boots off. Across from him sits a young woman in a borrowed hoodie, her hair wet, a blanket around her shoulders: THE STRANGER, early twenties. She holds a mug with both hands and has not spoken since the supply boat left her here.

                    PERPETUA
          Tea or something stronger?

The stranger shakes her head.

                    YOSHIRO
          She hasn't said a word.

                    PERPETUA
          She doesn't have to. She's drinking our tea.

The kettle shrieks. Perpetua lifts it off the plate. The platform groans against a swell, and the tea in the mug trembles in rings.

                    YOSHIRO
          Supply boat's not back till Thursday.

                    PERPETUA
          Then she's our guest till Thursday.

                    YOSHIRO
          Perp, we don't have a bunk.

                    PERPETUA
          Take mine.

                    YOSHIRO
          I can't take

                    PERPETUA
          Yoshiro.

He raises both hands in surrender. The stranger sets down her mug and, for the first time, looks up at them.

                    THE STRANGER
          Adebola.

Perpetua and Yoshiro turn. The word hangs in the steam.

                    PERPETUA
          Pardon?

                    ADEBOLA
          My name. Adebola Nwosu.

                    YOSHIRO
          Nice to meet you, Adebola.

                    ADEBOLA
          I should say I did not fall off the boat.

                    PERPETUA
          Did anyone say you did?

                    ADEBOLA
          I think you wondered.

Perpetua sets down the toast and wipes her hands on her trousers, slowly, one finger at a time.

                    PERPETUA
          We wondered.

                    ADEBOLA
          I walked off it.

                    YOSHIRO
          Walked off a moving boat.

                    ADEBOLA
          Into the sea, and then I swam here. It took a long time.

The room is very quiet. A pipe knocks in the wall. Yoshiro opens his mouth, closes it again.

                    PERPETUA
          Why?

Adebola turns the mug a quarter-turn on the table.

                    ADEBOLA
          I wanted to see if the platform was real. If anyone really lived out here.

                    YOSHIRO
          And?

                    ADEBOLA
          Someone made me tea.

Perpetua laughs, a startled bark. Then she pulls up a stool and sits.

                    PERPETUA
          Yoshiro, pour her another cup.

He fills it. Steam rises. The kettle ticks as it cools. Outside, the sea keeps its slow business.

                    PERPETUA (CONT'D)
          Adebola, you're going to want to eat something.

                    ADEBOLA
          I would like that.

                    YOSHIRO
          We have toast.

                    PERPETUA
          It's burnt.

                    ADEBOLA
          I will eat it burnt.
